			},
			"date": "2026-09-19T16:26:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@cwilcox808\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cwilcox808</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> MVC is often interoperable. </p><p>```<br>Page&amp;amp;nbsp;<br>```</p><p>Could have been a </p><p>```<br>padding-inline-end: 1ch;<br>```</p><p>For the record, and <a href=\"https://mas.to/tags/css\" class=\"mention hashtag\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#<span>css</span></a> content \"...\" is fitting markup-saving each and every line. It's special.</p>",
